## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ownership under pressure, bias-for-action with guardrails, and customer-first decision making when data signals risk.

## Key Concepts
- Ownership of a high-stakes feature
- Actionable rollout strategies with safe fallbacks
- Customer-obsession through measurable, segment-aware metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code: feature flag gating for checkout redesign
const FEATURE_FLAG = getFlag('checkoutRedesign');
if (FEATURE_FLAG && isMobileUser()) {
  showNewCheckout();
} else {
  showOldCheckout();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design rollback instrumentation to ensure rapid detection?
- How would you communicate risk trade-offs to leadership without slowing progress?

